{"step_index":191,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T05:42:50Z","content":"I have generated a formal **Software Requirements Specification (SRS)** document for the **SecureChain Software Supply Chain Security Platform** adhering to **IEEE Std 830 / ISO/IEC/IEEE 29148** standards.\n\nYou can view the full document here: [srs_document.md](file:///c:/Users/addal/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2ac62f09-2e24-4efd-bd40-62368c77dbf2/srs_document.md)\n\n---\n\n### 📄 SRS Executive Summary\n\n#### 1. System Scope\nSecureChain governs the end-to-end software pipeline:\n$$\\text{Developer} \\longrightarrow \\text{Source Repository} \\longrightarrow \\text{Build Environment} \\longrightarrow \\text{Dependencies} \\longrightarrow \\text{Security Scan} \\longrightarrow \\text{Artifact Repository}$$\n\n#### 2. Functional Requirements Highlight\n* **FR-1 (Project & Dependency Graph)**: Registration of projects across `NPM`, `PyPI`, `Maven`, `Go`, `Cargo`, `Docker`, tracking direct/transitive dependencies up to arbitrary depths.\n* **FR-2 (Scanner Engine & Risk Score)**: Asynchronous scanner engine calculating a normalized risk score ($0.0 - 100.0$):\n  $$\\text{RiskScore} = \\min\\left(100.0, \\frac{40 \\cdot N_{\\text{crit}} + 20 \\cdot N_{\\text{high}} + 8 \\cdot N_{\\text{med}} + 2 \\cdot N_{\\text{low}}}{120.0} \\times 100\\right)$$\n* **FR-3 (Targeted Threat Capabilities)**:\n  1. **Dependency Confusion**: Detects private/internal packages resolving to public registries without namespace isolation.\n  2. **Malicious Package Detection**: Matches packages against known threat intel feeds (`event-stream`, `node-ipc`, `xz-utils`).\n  3. **Artifact Tampering**: Verifies SHA-256 digests and flags tampered binaries.\n  4. **Build Compromise**: Evaluates SLSA build provenance data.\n  5. **Secret Leakage**: Scans CI build logs for leaked credentials (AWS keys, GitHub tokens, RSA private keys).\n  6. **Transitive Graph Analysis**: Flags deep transitive dependency graphs ($\\text{depth} \\ge 5$).\n* **FR-4 (Artifact Integrity)**: Registries Cosign cryptographic signing status and SHA-256 checksums.\n* **FR-5 (Remediation Lifecycle)**: Tracks vulnerability resolutions (`Open` $\\rightarrow$ `In Progress` $\\rightarrow$ `Resolved`).\n* **FR-6 (CycloneDX SBOM Reports)**: Generates CycloneDX v1.4 compliant Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) JSON reports.\n\n#### 3. Security Controls & STRIDE Matrix\n* **Spoofing**: Cosign cryptographic signatures.\n* **Tampering**: SHA-256 hash pinning for packages & build artifacts.\n* **Information Disclosure**: RegEx secret scanners redacting credentials in build logs.\n* **Elevation of Privilege**: Internal namespace scoping controls."}
